--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI DrivingDynamicsPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable DrivingDynamicsDataSource seam whose methods
keep the web hook names at the Swift call sites (useMotorLatest ← GET /motor/latest, useMotorHistory ←
GET /motor, useDrives ← GET /drives?vehicle_id, useDrivingCoach ← GET /analytics/driving-coach,
useDriveDynamicsLatest ← GET /drive-dynamics/latest, useVehicleState ← GET /vehicles/{id}/state,
useSignalObservations ← GET /signals/observations, loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle/GET /vehicles).

The web client-side derivations (computeMotorStats, getThrottleStyle, the SpeedGear/DriveAnalytics/
DrivingTips/DrivingCoach useMemo blocks) are ported verbatim into the deterministic, harness-tested
DrivingDynamicsEngine. SI stays canonical in the model (N·m, rpm, °C, W, Wh, m, m·s⁻¹); conversion to
the user's unit preference happens ONLY at the SwiftUI render boundary via the shared Units facade +
DynamicsFormat (ADR-005).

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global VehicleSelect) and ALL
of the web `space-y-6` sections, in the same data + grouping + order:

  LiveMotorStatus (GlassPanel — torque/front-rpm/motor-temp gauges + shift chip, or "awaiting" empty),
  GForcePanel (GlassPanel — lateral/longitudinal/combined G stat cards, or empty),
  PedalUsage (GlassPanel — throttle/brake gauges + brake-active chip, or empty),
  SpeedGearPanel (GlassPanel — shift / motor power / avg + top drive speed),
  AutopilotSection (GlassPanel — current/cruise speed + follow distance, or empty),
  MotorHistoryCharts (3 ChartContainers — power area, torque line, rpm line; each with its empty),
  MotorEfficiencyInsights (3 GlassPanels — torque distribution / throttle behavior / motor thermal),
  SummaryStats (6 StatCards — readings / avg torque / peak power / peak regen / avg power / avg temp),
  DrivingCoachSection (score gauge, style-breakdown bar, efficiency stats, weekly-trend line chart,
    pattern indicators, recommendations list, sortable per-drive table — each with its empty),
  DriveAnalyticsSection (the date RangePicker, speed-distribution bar, acceleration scatter, power
    profile dual-area),
  DrivingTips (GlassPanel — the driving-style recommendation list).

Charts use the P3 native Swift Charts wrappers (TSAreaChart/TSLineChart/TSBarChart/TSScatterChart),
never a WKWebView. Adaptive across macOS/iPad regular width vs. iPhone compact (ADR-002/006): the gauge
grids, the G-force / pedal / autopilot stat rows, the efficiency-insight row, the summary-stat grid,
the coach grids, and the analytics chart row all reflow via the isCompact flag. Every visible literal
resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (zero hardcoded text). All three data states
(loading skeleton / retryable error / success) are implemented; every section additionally carries its
own empty state so the page is never globally blank (web renders all panels unconditionally).

There is no map (manifest declares 0 maps). The web data sources are polled request/response (TanStack
refetchInterval), not SSE streams, so — as the sibling DriveScorePage records — no >2 min SSE staleness
indicator applies; refresh is wired through .refreshable + .task.

